# 🔍 How the Network Sniffer Works

The program uses Scapy to listen for network packets.

When a packet is captured, the program checks whether it contains an IP layer.

If an IP packet is detected, the program extracts:

```text
Source IP
Destination IP
Protocol
Source Port
Destination Port
Payload
```

The program then displays this information in the terminal.

